{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966793,"nonce":"dBOaJyDROExqFvabxt4Lo3cC7eI=","title":"gpu-alloc 0.6.1 was published as a patch but introduces a breaking AsRef\u003cMD\u003e bound that","message":"`gpu-alloc 0.6.1` was published as a patch version but adds a breaking\n`AsRef\u003cMD\u003e` bound on `GpuAllocator::{alloc, dealloc, cleanup}`.\n`wgpu-hal 26.0.5` calls those methods with `\u0026*self.shared` where\n`self.shared: Arc\u003cDeviceShared\u003e` and `DeviceShared` does not implement\n`AsRef\u003cgpu_alloc::Device\u003e` — every call site errors with\n`the trait AsRef\u003c_\u003e is not implemented for DeviceShared`.\n\nLocally `Cargo.lock` pins `gpu-alloc 0.6.0`, so dev builds pass. CI's\n`scripts/ci-strip-local-patch.sh` removes the `[patch]` block for\n`packages/*` git URLs before cargo runs. The Cargo.toml mutation\ninvalidates the lock entries for the patched subtree (canvas_kit /\nportal_ui / node_editor) and cargo re-resolves, picking\n`gpu-alloc 0.6.1` from the semver range `wgpu-hal` declares.\n\n**Why:** upstream incorrectly versioned a breaking change as a patch.\nWe can't keep cargo from re-resolving when `[patch]` entries are\nstripped on CI, so we have to constrain the version at the workspace\nlevel.\n\n**How to apply:** pin `gpu-alloc = \"=0.6.0\"` in\n`[workspace.dependencies]` and declare `gpu-alloc.workspace = true` in\n`blinc_gpu/Cargo.toml` so the constraint propagates without a source\nimport (same pattern as the `wgpu-hal = \"=26.0.5\"` pin documented\ninline at the workspace `Cargo.toml`). Watch for an upstream\n`gpu-alloc 0.6.2` that reverts or a `wgpu-hal` patch release that\nabsorbs the new bound — when either ships, the pin can move.\n\nCompanion to [[gotcha-wgpu-hal-26-0-6-acquire-regression]]: same\npattern (transitive-dep pin via direct workspace dep on a crate that\ndoesn't import the symbol).","files":null}]}